WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.606 --> 00:00:06.113 line:10%
Hey everybody, we are here in London
at the Long Cross studios

00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:10.784 line:10%
to visit the set of <i>Now You See Me 2</i>.
This is the sequel to the 2013,

00:00:10.784 --> 00:00:13.144 line:90%
incredibly successful,
bank heist flick.

00:00:13.494 --> 00:00:16.626 line:90%
So, how did they pull off all
of those incredible illusions?

00:00:16.726 --> 00:00:19.494 line:90%
Well, that's what we're here
to find out. Let's go inside.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:23.488 line:10%
My magic trick here is when
I want things to disappear,

00:00:23.488 --> 00:00:25.080 line:10%
I just say, "Cut."

00:00:25.928 --> 00:00:27.933 line:90%
What? (LAUGHING)

00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:31.278 line:10%
When I do it it's just magic
and then you just

00:00:31.278 --> 00:00:33.346 line:10%
-go like that or just point to it.
-(LAUGHING)

00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:35.506 line:10%
I'm here with Dave Franco.
So this is obviously

00:00:35.506 --> 00:00:36.875 line:10%
-your second time back.
-Yes.

00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:40.100 line:90%
How does it feel being back on set
with some of the same actors?

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.402 line:90%
DAVE: It's very uncomfortable.
It's just a lot of man love,

00:00:43.653 --> 00:00:45.242 line:90%
-and uh--
-(LAUGHING)

00:00:45.242 --> 00:00:46.830 line:90%
I thought you were about to say
it's uncomfortable,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.315 line:90%
and you don't like the cast.
(LAUGHING)

00:00:48.315 --> 00:00:50.027 line:90%
-No, no, no.
-But the level of love

00:00:50.027 --> 00:00:51.316 line:90%
-is uncomfortable.
-Yes, exactly.

00:00:51.316 --> 00:00:53.098 line:90%
Probably makes everyone around us
uncomfortable.

00:00:57.701 --> 00:01:00.319 line:90%
Did you ever expect to be here again
filming a second part?

00:01:00.319 --> 00:01:03.100 line:90%
JESSE: It didn't cross my mind,
but it's the kind of movie

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.014 line:90%
that can lend itself to a sequel
'cause it's all created mythology.

00:01:07.195 --> 00:01:09.883 line:90%
You know, it takes place
in this world that's both

00:01:10.158 --> 00:01:14.223 line:90%
of the real world and also created,
so it makes sense that the story

00:01:14.223 --> 00:01:16.154 line:90%
<i>can continue past where
the first one ended.</i>

00:01:16.154 --> 00:01:18.640 line:90%
TIFFANY: How does it feel being
the new kid on the block

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.962 line:10%
with everybody who's worked
on it,

00:01:19.962 --> 00:01:22.532 line:10%
who has a little more
practice already with the magic?

00:01:22.532 --> 00:01:24.677 line:10%
Oh, I've already lapped them
when it comes to magic.

00:01:24.677 --> 00:01:25.865 line:90%
-What?
-Yeah, instantly.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.019 line:90%
Uh, no, it doesn't--
I guess it's a--

00:01:28.019 --> 00:01:31.726 line:90%
It's a testament to how fun
this job is that I keep forgetting

00:01:31.726 --> 00:01:34.444 line:90%
that I wasn't in the first one
and that I'm the new person.

00:01:34.444 --> 00:01:35.899 line:10%
With a movie,
there's many different tricks

00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:39.072 line:10%
and we're so used to crazy
visual effects, that we really put

00:01:39.072 --> 00:01:41.817 line:10%
a lot of pressure on making sure
that everything was practical

00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.842 line:90%
and that when you see it,
we're not cutting around;

00:01:43.842 --> 00:01:46.858 line:90%
we're not cheating you.
Uh, that you actually get

00:01:46.858 --> 00:01:49.139 line:90%
to experience the magic
as if you were there in person.

00:01:49.139 --> 00:01:51.188 line:90%
And use the friction
to kind of flick it up.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.148 line:90%
-Perfect. Perfect.
-(LAUGHING)

00:01:54.148 --> 00:01:56.612 line:90%
Dave is actually amazing.

00:01:57.573 --> 00:01:58.823 line:90%
-What?
-Pretty cool, huh?

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:03.305 line:90%
JON: I thought it was not possible
from an actor on, in camera.

00:02:03.305 --> 00:02:07.307 line:90%
Uh, the truth is all the really great
illusions in the movie,

00:02:07.307 --> 00:02:13.176 line:90%
uh, are hand doubles, people who are
really wonderful like this man here.

00:02:13.176 --> 00:02:17.478 line:90%
(LAUGHING) Do you want him
to be your hand double

00:02:17.478 --> 00:02:18.689 line:90%
-for this interview?
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:18.689 --> 00:02:22.060 line:90%
I heard that you actually
have been working a little bit

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.814 line:90%
-on the mentalist side?
-(LAUGHING)

00:02:23.814 --> 00:02:26.891 line:90%
-Or like...mind readings? (LAUGHING)
-No, I'm horrible.

00:02:26.891 --> 00:02:29.076 line:90%
I'm the worst at it,
but hopefully one day

00:02:29.076 --> 00:02:31.110 line:90%
I can hypnotize somebody
in some way.

00:02:31.418 --> 00:02:34.068 line:90%
Come see the movie.
Come see the movie.

00:02:34.068 --> 00:02:35.272 line:90%
It's really great.

